   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Hi All,<br>\n</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">I just\nrealize that the mcmcsamp function of lme4 was not implemented for the new\nversion of lme4. <br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Bit of a pain in the b** for the code I am using for my dugong\ndensity analysis. <br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Can anyone tell me how I can get around this? I am new to R\nand thus have very little experience.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That\nwould be VERY helpful, thanks.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Christophe Cleguer</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><br></span></p>\n\n</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tVM3O3yZwXkJ",
   "from": "Craigie, Ian",
   "author": "2d3be3445f567d23",
   "date": "2014-01-07T05:00:02Z",
   "subject": "RE: [Trop-R] mcmcsamp function no longer operational ...",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Christophe,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">You ask a good question because the loss of that function is going to be a serious headache for a number of people, including me.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">The quickest solution is probably to install an older version of R and the associated packages you need so you can run your existing code. There is a description\r\n of how to do this here: </span><a href=\"http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/How-to-install-older-version-of-R-td889239.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/How-to-install-older-version-of-R-td889239.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793246297227000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1sQZruwF4udbbrD8j_NNvb\">http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/How-to-install-older-version-of-R-td889239.html</a> .\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">It’s a bit of a fiddle because each package has to be downloaded and installed manually but it’s not difficult. File versions dated around the middle of 2013 should be about right.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">In the longer term we’ll have to use one of the alternative methods suggested under ‘pvalues’ on p59 in the lme4 pdf:\r\n</span><a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/lme4/lme4.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/lme4/lme4.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793246297227000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0cIfdDdLd10-FId-F0gouC\">http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/lme4/lme4.pdf</a> .<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Getting p-values from mixed effect models with mcmcsamp has always been statistically iffy, and it’s a hangover from older modelling methods that has led to\r\n a desire to produce them for reviewers and editors etc. <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Hope that helps,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Ian</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#365f91\">Ian Craigie Ph.D.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#365f91\">Postdoctoral Research Fellow<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#365f91\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#365f91\">ARC Centre of Excellence for Coral Reef Studies,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#365f91\">James Cook University, Townsville, QLD 4811, Australia<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#365f91\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#365f91\">Phone: +61 042 590 4667\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#365f91\"><a href=\"http://www.coralcoe.org.au/\" title=\"blocked::http://www.coralcoe.org.au/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.coralcoe.org.au/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793246297227000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1lRn2xHe77GmZv7kja8yBe\"><span style=\"color:#365f91\">http://www.coralcoe.org.au/</span></a></span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#17365d\"><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">From:</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tropi...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tropi...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Christophe Cleguer<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Tuesday, 7 January 2014 2:21 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tropi...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [Trop-R] mcmcsamp function no longer operational ...<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\">Hi All,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I just realize that the mcmcsamp function of lme4 was not implemented for the new version of lme4.\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Bit of a pain in the b** for the code I am using for my dugong density analysis.\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Can anyone tell me how I can get around this? I am new to R and thus have very little experience.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">That would be VERY helpful, thanks.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Christophe Cleguer<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
